  "text_pages": [
    "Preparing for your stay - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nGo to content\nGo to search\nGo to menu\nPreparing for your stay - Bordeaux Montaigne University v1.2\nShare\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nSend by Mail\nYour name\n*\nYour mail\n*\nRecipient(s)\n*\nSeparated by coma\nMessage\nImage's text\n*\nIf the image is not clear enough, you can refresh the page.\nPreparing for your stay\nAccomodation\nYou can arrange your accommodation in different ways for the stay at\nBordeaux Montaigne University: university residences or renting/sharing\na flat.\nDue to its quality of life, Bordeaux is a very attractive city and students might have trouble finding an accommodation\n.\nWe strongly recommend to find an accommodation independently before your arrival in Bordeaux. Different types of housing are available. We suggest to visit our partner's platform:\nhttps://u-bordeaux-montaigne.studapart.com/fr/\nStudent residences on Campus (“CROUS residences”): Interested students can apply for a CROUS accommodation. Student must complete the CROUS application form at the earliest convenience on \"\nMes Services étudiants\n\" web site (For further details, please find attached our calendar) and send an email to Mr David CAZENAVE, administrative officer - Student Mobility Office (International Affairs) before May 31 : david.cazenave@u-bordeaux-montaigne.fr\nPlease note that a very limited number of CROUS (spots are limited) accommodations is available for students on an exchange program.\nFor further information about accomodation: find accomodation, home insurance, advices and tips\nhere\nInternational Welcome Desk\nLocated at the heart of Montaigne Campus, the International Welcome Desk guides our 2,500 international students on their first steps in the French Higher Education system, whether they are exchange students or not.\nFor further information about visa, banks and money transfers, health insurance, transports and our buddy system...visit our pages\nhere\nfooter-script"
  ],
